# =============================================================================
# Repo-root .dockerignore — applies ONLY to builds that use the repo root as the
# build context. Today that is the *release* image path:
#   .github/workflows/release.yml -> api/Dockerfile.release, gateway/Dockerfile.release
# (both `context: .`). The release images bake the repo-root `skills/` corpus and
# `gateway.yaml.example`, which the dev stack bind-mounts instead.
#
# The dev builds (docker-compose.yml: build.context ./api, ./gateway, ./web) use
# subdir contexts and their OWN api/.dockerignore, gateway/.dockerignore,
# web/.dockerignore — this file does NOT affect them.
#
# Patterns are matched against paths relative to the build context root (repo
# root). Root-anchored patterns (leading `/`) match only at the top level so we
# don't strip load-bearing `.md` files (SKILL.md, api/README.md, gateway/README.md)
# from inside skills/, api/, gateway/.
# =============================================================================

# ----- VCS + CI (never belong in an image) -----
/.git
/.github

# ----- Subsystems not part of the api/gateway release images -----
# web is built from its own ./web context (not repo-root) — don't ship its
# sources into the api/gateway images.
/web
/desktop
/word-addin
/slack-bridge
/teams-bridge
/deploy
/docs
/tests
/scripts

# ----- Compose + release artifacts -----
/docker-compose*.yml
**/*.spdx.json

# ----- Root-level docs (keep SKILL.md etc. inside skills/) -----
/*.md

# ----- macOS Finder duplicate files -----
# On iCloud-synced filesystems, Finder occasionally creates phantom duplicates
# named "foo 2.py", "foo 3.py", etc. These break Alembic ("Multiple head
# revisions") and Python imports when they sneak into the build context.
**/* [0-9].*
**/* [0-9][0-9].*

# Finder filesystem metadata.
**/.DS_Store
**/._*

# ----- Python build / test caches (never belong in the image) -----
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/

# ----- Local virtualenvs -----
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/env/

# ----- Node modules (web is excluded above; this covers any stray copies) -----
**/node_modules/

# ----- Editor / OS detritus -----
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/

# ----- Misc -----
*.log
